<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Molson makes deal with Coors - Foster's.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Molson makes deal with Coors - Foster's.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foster's Brewing Group Ltd said on Thursday its 40 percent owned Canada-based Molson Cos Ltd had reached an agreement with U.S. beer maker Adolph Coors Co to brew Coors beer until June 1997.</p>
<p>This follows an Canadian arbitration panel decision on October 20 that Molson had relinguished all rights to brew Coors products in 1993 when Philip Morris Co bought an interest in the Canadian brewer.</p>
<p>Molson said the agreement would reduce its earnings by C$15 million for the period from October 18, 1996 to June 30, 1997.</p>
</text>
